# Floating list pages

A short page of captions, values, badges and switches is a
`GroupedListWidget`. Copy an existing page. Do not add another way
to size, refresh or measure it.

Models: `ReplayDialog.cpp` (shortest floating dialog),
`WindSettingsDialog.cpp` (live values and switches),
`Panels/WindConfigPanel.cpp` (configuration page).

## Floating dialog

`WidgetDialog::Floating` takes the list and no width. Add the
buttons, call `PrepareFloatingList()`, fill the values, then
`ShowModal()`. `RefitList()` reads `PreferredTextWidth()`.

```cpp
auto *list = new GroupedListWidget(look);
WidgetDialog dialog(WidgetDialog::Floating{}, parent, look,
                    _("Title"), list);
dialog.AddButton(_("Close"), mrOK);
dialog.PrepareFloatingList();
setup.Refresh();
dialog.ShowModal();
```

## Rows, added once

`AddValue(caption, help, value, edit)` stores the row.
`UpdateValues()` calls `value` again. Call `RefitList()` only when
that returns true. A value that still fits is redrawn in place.

`value` fills a `ValueState`. Assign `state.text` before the call
returns; the list copies it. A badge pointer is a `_()` literal.
`state.help == nullptr` leaves the explanation passed to
`AddValue`. That text sits below the settings when the rows and
the text both fit. When the page scrolls, or the text does not
fit there, it sits under the selected row. `state.hidden` drops
the row. `state.disabled` greys a row that has `edit`.

No `edit`: the row stays grey and the cursor may rest so the
explanation can be read. With `edit`: the label selects, the value
opens, and Enter still opens the row.

A status row the cursor must skip (the wind source) is `AddItem`
with `.disabled = true` and a `value_callback`. `AddValue` would
leave it selectable.

A switch is `AddItem` once, with `.toggle = true`. The callback
flips the model bool and does not rebuild the list. Keep those
bools until Close or `Save()`.

## Configuration page

The page is the list. `Create*()` returns a `GroupedListWidget`
with `SetSaveCallback`. That callback writes the settings when
the configuration dialogue closes. There is no forwarding wrapper.

`AddSwitch(caption, help, field)` flips `field`. Pass `expert`
to hide the row until expert mode is on, and `shown` to hide it
while a predicate is false. `AddEnum` and `AddText` store the
value and open the existing picker. A number is `AddInteger` or
`AddFloat`. A file or password stays `AddValue` with the dialog
that page already used.

`ConfigPanel::CommitSetting` writes one setting and, with a key,
its profile entry. Keep the values in a `shared_ptr` until the
save callback runs.

The configuration dialogue already wraps the page in
`VScrollWidget`. Leave the list's minimum and maximum size as
they are. That outer scroller stays idle, and the list draws a
bar only when the rows, including an open explanation, do not fit.

## Leave the shared list alone

`Clear()` still rebuilds device and weather lists. These pages do
not use it to change a value. An explanation that already exists
in `po/xcsoar.pot` stays that msgid.
